From 6d063326334df246bb29ef5b32593510cfdb9acc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:56:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Estimate kernel stack sizes on SROA'd IR

With HOST_CPU_ENABLE_STACK_SIZE_CHECK, CL_KERNEL_WORK_GROUP_SIZE is
limited by an estimate of each kernel's per-work-item stack use, taken
from the linked program before any optimization. The kernel library is
built at -O0, so that counted every local variable of every builtin a
kernel calls: 1.5 KiB for hypot(double), 9 KiB for tgamma(double), all of
which the kernel compiler's optimizations remove. With the 384 KiB budget
of a macOS worker thread, a kernel calling hypot was limited to 259
work-items, while its work-group function for 256 work-items needs about
2 KiB of stack.

Estimate on a copy of the program that went through SROA instead.
Allocas that survive it, like dynamically indexed private arrays, still
count. With -cl-opt-disable, which turns off the kernel compiler's
optimizations, the estimate stays on the unoptimized program.

The estimate moves from link(), which the JIT also uses to link
work-group functions, to the program build, where it is read, and only
runs for devices that use it.
